Ronald the barbarian was turning into quite the 'ole character when he
reached the 10th level of the dungeonds of doom. His long sword
demonbane and +1 two-handed sword, while not the most effective in the
world, cut down many a foe. 

With his trusty housecat, he creeps down the stairs to the 10th level in
his boots of stealth. What does he see? No problem... a plains centaur.
Sounds like another notch on the belt. The battle went something like
this: The plains centaur zaps a wand...the death ray hits Rexx's
ghost...the death ray hits you...you die...But wait...the amulet around
your neck begins to glow...You are saved...The amulet crumbles to dust
(so that's what that unidentified amulet was, I think thankfully). The
death ray bounces...the death ray hits you...YOU DIE! Boy, I'm sure glad
the walls in this game that wreak more havoc than the monsters.  
